UPDATE lpm_schema_elements SET metadata = jsonb_set(jsonb_set(metadata, '{aligned_stages}', coalesce(metadata->'aligned_stages', '[]'::jsonb) || '[{"stage_id":"396e3dd9-4f22-5160-b6c7-3752caefa1b8","stage":"I4:9-12 Selection Across Biology, Culture, Education, and AI","relation":"related","strength":"weak","why":"Information station of int: Students fill one analogy map for four receivers: a bacterium, a bird hearing song, a reader of a news post","sense_differs":null,"adjacent_band":false,"source":"information-strategy"}]'::jsonb), '{alignment_state}', '"aligned"') WHERE id = 'ecfcc7aa-f46a-56fe-97c6-1a7a71acf4df' AND NOT (coalesce(metadata->'aligned_stages', '[]'::jsonb) @> '[{"stage_id":"396e3dd9-4f22-5160-b6c7-3752caefa1b8"}]'::jsonb);
UPDATE projects SET introduction = introduction || '

Information. This space treats information in its own terms. Information is a pattern that varies in step with something else. It becomes information for a receiver that can use the link. What the receiver makes of it, the response or expectation it triggers, is its meaning for that receiver. Whether a sender, an intention or a bit count applies differs by domain. The space joins the disciplinary readings and says where a shared word stops meaning the same thing. This strategy makes that its main work and models the paper''s recommendations: the three dimensions in the paper''s order, with the step from structure to meaning as the central contribution. Stations 5, 6 and 10 fill a table of where the shared word breaks. Perception and sensing get a home that no stage carried. Anything beyond biology is the design''s own extension of the paper. The paper''s order is kept. K-2 sorts patterns nobody sent from patterns made to tell. Grades 3-5 compare what different receivers can pick up and ask who sends a passed-on pattern. Grades 6-8 ask what shaped the receiver and what the pattern means to it: cue, signal, honesty, bit counts. Grades 9-12 remove the controller and test where sender, receiver and meaning stop applying. Evolution enters at 3-5 and returns at 6-8 and 9-12. Dimension 3 starts at 9-12 because evidence for younger students is thin. The strategy rests on the paper by Eirdosh and Hanisch (2026, in press) and is a proposal. AI drafted it and no subject expert has reviewed it.' WHERE id = '371fce26-d1f3-439b-95df-0a0e38b8a824' AND introduction NOT LIKE '%Information. This space treats information in its own terms.%';
